    {
      "field_name": "diagnostic_criteria",
      "value": "The prodrome involves (a) stiffness and rigidity in axial muscles; (b) slow progression of stiffness to proximal limbs, making volitional movements and ambulation difficult; (c) a fixed spine deformity contributing to pronounced lordosis; (d) superimposed episodic spasms precipitated by sudden movement, loud noise, or emotional upset; (e) normal findings on motor and sensory nerve examinations; (f) normal intellect; (g) electromyographic findings typical of continuous motor activity that is responsive to diazepam; and (h) seropositive results for antiglutamic acid decarboxylase (anti-GAD65) autoantibodies.",
